/-
  E8TrialityCertVI.lean —  "3 does not divide 8".

  The obstruction behind Cert IV, and its absence at order 4.

  * Section N (obstruction).  sigma is the fixed-point-free order-3 permutation
    x |-> (x+1)/(-x) of P^1(F_23) = 24 points, an automorphism of the Golay code.
    Its orbits all have size 3 and partition the 24 points.  Any sigma-invariant
    subset is a union of orbits, hence has cardinality divisible by 3.  Since
    3 does not divide 8, NO 8-element subset is sigma-invariant -- in particular
    no Golay octad.  Verified twice: over the 256 unions of orbits, and by an
    exhaustive sweep of all 2^24 subsets.
    Consequence: the octad-block construction, which hands every order-2 and
    order-4 element a commuting EE8-involution for free, cannot even be attempted
    for sigma.  That is why Cert IV needed an exhaustive 4-clique sweep.

  * Section O (no obstruction at order 4).  Representatives of the three order-4
    classes of M_24 (cycle types 1^4 2^2 4^4, 2^4 4^4, 4^6) each stabilise an
    octad: 11, 7 and 3 of them respectively.  Orbits have sizes 1, 2, 4 -- all
    divisors of 8.

  * Section P (the lattice witness).  For g the permutation isometry of Leech
    given by the 4^6 element: Fix(g) is nontrivial, the Turyn block M_O of a
    g-invariant octad is sqrt2*E8, g preserves it, and the resulting involution
    eps has trace 8 and commutes with g.

  Pure Lean 4 core; all proofs by native_decide.
  NOTE: `no_sigma_invariant_eight_set` sweeps 2^24 masks and is the heaviest
  check in the project; `orbit_unions_never_eight` is the cheap moral content.
-/
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000

abbrev Mat := List (List Int)
/-- `List.get!` was removed from this Lean core; reintroduce it locally. -/
def List.get! {α : Type _} [Inhabited α] (l : List α) (n : Nat) : α := l.getD n default
def dot (a b : List Int) : Int := (List.zipWith (fun x y => x*y) a b).foldl (fun s x => s+x) 0
def col (A : Mat) (j : Nat) : List Int := A.map (fun r => r.get! j)
def tr (A : Mat) : Mat := (List.range ((A.get! 0).length)).map (col A)
def mul (A B : Mat) : Mat := let Bt := tr B; A.map (fun r => Bt.map (fun c => dot r c))
def idm (n : Nat) : Mat := (List.range n).map (fun i => (List.range n).map (fun j => if i = j then (1:Int) else 0))
def negm (A : Mat) : Mat := A.map (fun r => r.map (fun x => -x))
def smul (c : Int) (A : Mat) : Mat := A.map (fun r => r.map (fun x => c*x))
def trace (A : Mat) : Int := ((List.range A.length).map (fun i => (A.get! i).get! i)).foldl (fun s x => s+x) 0
def evenDiag (A : Mat) : Bool := (List.range A.length).all (fun i => ((A.get! i).get! i) % 2 == 0)
def rowMul (r : List Int) (A : Mat) : List Int := (tr A).map (fun c => dot r c)

